            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="d60-03" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve13/d60-03"/>

                <head>61. Note From the President’s Deputy Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Haig) to the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger),
                    Washington, November 18, 1971<anchor n="1" xml:id="d61-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d61-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1971-11-18"
                        >November 18, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d61-01" n="1" xml:id="d61-01"/>
                <p>November 18, 1971</p>
                <p> Henry:</p>
                <p> Walters saw Group 2—was cordially received. Their Number One is back. He stated
                    that the Chinese strongly prefer 29 November rather than 23 November for
                    announcement. They explained that the problem involved the fact that they will
                    have a visitor from Hanoi in Peking on the 23d and, therefore, hope that we can
                    make the announcement on the 29th.</p>
                <p>There were no answers on additional details and no indication of when they would
                    have such an answer. However, they expressed great gratitude that the U.S. side
                    had agreed to the seven-day trip. They expressed pleasure that the First Lady
                    would come and that the President will travel in their aircraft. The Chinese
                    Ambassador was also anxious to know when he could see you and Walters indicated
                    that this depended on the North Vietnamese.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> AL HAIG </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 849,
                    President’s File-China Trip, China Exchanges, Oct 20, 1971-Dec 31, 1971. Top
                    Secret; Sensitive.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d61-f2" n="2" xml:id="d61-f2-content">
                <p> Haig relayed Military Attaché Walters’s information concerning the announcement
                    of President Nixon’s China trip.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
